1 NAME Nellie Florence /Bowland/
2 GIVN Nellie Florence
2 SURN Bowland
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 SEP 1904
2 PLAC Tiffin, Seneca County, Ohio
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1991
2 PLAC Park Forest, Cook County, Illinois
1 BURI
2 PLAC Chapel Hill Gardens South, Worth, Cook County, Illinois
1 NOTE SCHMIDTISTICS tier: confirmed
1 NOTE Upgraded from the delta a1758 placeholder (no facts asserted) using three sources directly viewed this delta: N-28 (The Wetmore Spectator, 6 Nov 1925 -- a marriage-license announcement, not a report of the ceremony itself, so marriage_date is carried as 'Abt 6 Nov 1925' rather than an exact day; lists Kenneth's age as 21, though his own confirmed 04 Oct 1905 birth makes him 20 at the time -- a one-year discrepancy, not pursued); N-29 (Chicago Tribune, 3 May 1991 -- her own death/funeral notice, naming surviving husband Kenneth, all three children by name, a previously-unknown sister Annie Ferguson -- see open_lead 649 -- two further late sisters and two late brothers, unnamed, and burial at Chapel Hill Gardens South; this cemetery is given as 'Oak Lawn' at G-28 and 'Worth' here -- the same cemetery, two adjoining suburbs' names, not a conflict); and M-34 (U.S
2 CONT Social Security Applications and Claims Index -- gives birth 16 Sep 1904, Tiffin, Seneca County, Ohio, correcting the 'Adams County' figure repeated across three never-viewed raw-GEDCOM citations, see conflicts seq 185, settled -- and independently confirms parents William A
2 CONT Bowland and Mary Porter, matching the raw GEDCOM's own FAMC record)
2 CONT death is written as '1991' (year only): N-29's own funeral-notice timeline (published and scheduling burial 3-4 May 1991) contradicts the raw GEDCOM / M-34's stated Death Date of 10 May 1991 by a full week -- see conflicts seq 184, left OPEN, not adjudicated -- so neither day is asserted here
2 CONT Full SSN digits (visible on M-34, matching the partial figure already sitting unpromoted in the raw GEDCOM) and the index's 'Race' field are deliberately not logged, as not relevant to the birth/marriage/death basics open_lead 647 asked for
2 CONT Resolves open_lead 647 in full.
1 NOTE SCHMIDTISTICS source(s): N-28, N-29, M-34
